{"slug":"/references/settings/listAndCountPropertyLabels","title":"listAndCountPropertyLabels - Settings Module Reference","frontmatter":{"displayed_sidebar":"settingsReference","slug":"/references/settings/listAndCountPropertyLabels","sidebar_label":"listAndCountPropertyLabels"},"toc":[{"title":"Example","id":"example","level":2},{"title":"Parameters","id":"listandcountpropertylabels-parameters","level":2},{"title":"Returns","id":"listandcountpropertylabels-returns","level":2}],"blocks":[{"kind":"markdown","html":"This documentation provides a reference to the `listAndCountPropertyLabels` method. This belongs to the Settings Module."},{"kind":"note","variant":"note","html":"You should only use this methods when implementing complex customizations. For common cases, check out [available workflows instead](/medusa-workflows-reference)."},{"kind":"markdown","html":"This method retrieves a paginated list of property labels along with the total count of available property labels satisfying the provided filters."},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example","id":"example"},{"kind":"markdown","html":"To retrieve a list of property labels using their IDs:\n\n```ts\nconst [propertyLabels, count] =\n  await settingsModuleService.listAndCountPropertyLabels({\n    id: [\"prlbl_123\", \"prlbl_321\"],\n  })\n```\n\nTo specify the fields to retrieve in each property label:\n\n```ts\nconst [propertyLabels, count] =\n  await settingsModuleService.listAndCountPropertyLabels(\n    {\n      id: [\"prlbl_123\", \"prlbl_321\"],\n    },\n    {\n      select: [\"id\", \"entity\", \"property\", \"label\"],\n    }\n  )\n```\n\nBy default, only the first `15` records are retrieved. You can control pagination by specifying the `skip` and `take` properties of the `config` parameter:\n\n```ts\nconst [propertyLabels, count] =\n  await settingsModuleService.listAndCountPropertyLabels(\n    {\n      entity: \"Product\",\n    },\n    {\n      take: 20,\n      skip: 2,\n    }\n  )\n```"},{"kind":"h